From 80622eaedbd75582f2483988c466f530674c6538 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:15:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] perf(loader): soak sub-2MiB buddy fragments across 4K and
 64K UMA kernels

Upstream base: local-inference-lab/vllm 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 (after candidate-54 0799).

Rationale:
In nvidia.ko (nv_alloc_system_pages), non-contiguous system-memory cuMemCreate allocations satisfy 20 MiB segments by draining smaller free physical buddy orders from 64 KiB upward (64K -> 128K -> 256K -> 512K -> 1M) before touching >= 2 MiB contiguous blocks. On GB10 (SM121, 24 MiB physically-indexed L2), scattered 64 KiB..256 KiB physical fragments self-conflict across L2 cache slices during 15-20 MiB decode L2 weight prefetches (+12-13% slower than >= 2 MiB contiguous blocks). Previously, _allocate_order13_sponge returned empty on all 4 KiB-page kernels and on 64 KiB-page kernels whenever 512 MiB (Order-13) blocks reached 0, and budgeted free memory from cudaMemGetInfo (MemFree) instead of UMA /proc/meminfo MemAvailable.

Changes:
- Generalize direct_loader.py buddy sponge across both 4 KiB and 64 KiB base page sizes (parse_buddyinfo_blocks, select_buddy_sponge_target, _available_uma_or_gpu_bytes): soak >= 64 KiB sub-2 MiB buddy fragments (or < 512 MiB when Order-13 blocks exist) bounded by UMA MemAvailable with a 10 GiB untouched floor so both the contiguous weight arena and MoE expert slabs draw directly from >= 2 MiB contiguous physical blocks on the first allocation, then release the sponge immediately.
- Bind contiguous weight arenas in DummyModelLoader.create_model on CUDA and zero non-floating-point dummy parameters on CUDA in initialize_single_dummy_weight.

Quality implications:
None. Weight values, dtypes, and kernel arithmetic are bit-identical.

Tests:
- pytest tests/model_executor/model_loader/test_direct_loader.py tests/model_executor/model_loader/test_direct_loader_cuda.py (88 passed on GB10).

Upstream status: spark-ds41f local candidate patch.
